    gsub(/[ `]/, "", $7); print $7 "  " p }' README.md | sha256sum -c
</code></pre> <p>Expect one <code>: OK</code> per row and exit 0. A <code>FAILED</code> line means the bytes on disk are not the ones the citations elsewhere in the repo were written against, which is a finding, not a filing error: re-open every row named in that document's "Cited by" column.</p> <p>Uses only <code>sub()</code> rather than gawk's three-argument <code>match()</code>, so it behaves the same under mawk, which is the default <code>awk</code> on Debian and Ubuntu.</p>
